                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='21273' id='18' type-v2='text' w='85333' x='667' y='62909'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='10'>KEY FINDINGS &amp; BUSINESS IMPLICATIONS</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>01 — API transactions have the highest failure rate</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>API transactions have a 6.57% failure rate, compared with 2.96% for Branch transactions. This suggests API payment flows deserve closer investigation.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>02 — Insufficient funds is the leading failure reason</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Of 2,296 failed transactions, 609 resulted from insufficient funds. Validation errors and timeouts are also significant contributors.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>03 — Processing times exhibit a long tail</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Median processing time is 26 seconds, while the 99th percentile reaches 727 seconds. This indicates substantial delays among a small subset of transactions.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>04 — Repeated payment references warrant investigation</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Across 50,000 synthetic transactions, 299 payment references appeared more than once, involving 599 transaction records. These occurrences warrant further review but do not independently establish duplicate charges or fraudulent activity.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#444444' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
